Well it finally happened.  I found 3.1.2 for the Mac.  And so I don't get
a ton of mail asking me where I found it, I'll tell you all now it was on
America Online and not an anonymous FTP site.  It may be located at one, but
unfortunately I don't know where.

Here it is.  I think 3.1.2's interface on the Mac is much better and it
seems to be more playable except for two problems, one minor and one major.

First, the walls and staircases and altars are all a light shade of gray 
that makes playing very hard on the eyes.  If anyone knows how to fix that I
would love to know.  

Second, the game crashes rather frequently.  This cannot be tolerated.  I
should tell you that I am on an LC II with 10 Meg Ram and using system 7.0.1.
I know the problem is not extention related because the game will still hang
or crash the system with all extensions turned off.

Since I am a devoted NetHackHead it seems a shame for me to suffer so...
Sigh...  But anyway, if anyone can help me out it would be greatly appreciated.

